From: PortCellar <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Recenter fully offscreen small windows.

Steam CEF login windows can request sentinel coordinates far outside the
visible desktop, then later become visible without ever crossing a macOS
screen. The existing bounds clamp keeps Cocoa inside documented coordinate
limits, but a clamped x/y of 16000 can still be invisible on normal desktop
sizes.

When a small window does not intersect the desktop at all, move it near the
desktop origin. This preserves large/fullscreen behavior and only handles the
fully offscreen small-window case.
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/window.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
index 54aa928..a6023c9 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -246,6 +246,14 @@ static void constrain_window_frame(CGRect* frame)
     if (frame->origin.y > 16000) frame->origin.y = 16000;
     if (frame->size.width > max_width) frame->size.width = max_width;
     if (frame->size.height > max_height) frame->size.height = max_height;
+
+    if (!CGRectIntersectsRect(*frame, desktop_rect) &&
+        frame->size.width <= CGRectGetWidth(desktop_rect) &&
+        frame->size.height <= CGRectGetHeight(desktop_rect))
+    {
+        frame->origin.x = CGRectGetMinX(desktop_rect) + 64;
+        frame->origin.y = CGRectGetMinY(desktop_rect) + 64;
+    }
 }
 
 
